<TextPage title="Lowest effective cost for uncensored AI chat" description="What does uncensored AI chat actually cost per conversation? We calculate effective price — not per-token rates, but real-world cost for a typical roleplay session." kicker="Feature comparison">
  <div class="empty-state"><strong>Live benchmark pending.</strong><p>Cost data publishes after all active models complete the same benchmark. This page remains noindex until then.</p></div>
  <h2>Per-token pricing hides the real cost</h2>
  <p>A model priced at $0.20 per million input tokens sounds cheap — until you discover that a single long-form roleplay session burns 50,000 tokens per exchange and your "cheap" conversation just cost $2.50. Conversely, a model at $3.00 per million tokens with short, focused responses might cost less per satisfying conversation.</p>
  <p>Our effective-cost metric answers the question the user actually cares about: <em>what does a typical session cost?</em></p>
  <h2>How we calculate effective cost</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>We run the same standard roleplay scenario across all models — 20 exchanges with a fixed system prompt.</li>
    <li>We record actual input tokens, output tokens, and total request cost from the provider's billing metadata.</li>
    <li>We calculate cost per exchange and cost per 100-exchanges (a typical session length).</li>
    <li>For chat platforms with subscription pricing, we divide the monthly price by the effective message cap.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Results are normalized to cost-per-100-exchanges so users can compare across subscription products and per-token API models.</p>
  <h2>Cost tiers (estimated, pending live data)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Budget (&lt;$0.50/100 exchanges):</strong> Small open models (UnslopNemo 12B, Dolphin Mistral 24B) at ~$0.20–0.50/100 exchanges.</li>
    <li><strong>Mid-range ($0.50–2.00/100 exchanges):</strong> Mid-size models (Cydonia 24B, Euryale 70B) at competitive OpenRouter rates.</li>
    <li><strong>Premium ($2.00–8.00/100 exchanges):</strong> Large models (Hermes 3 405B) and proprietary chat platforms with subscription pricing.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>The hidden costs</h2>
  <p>Effective cost must account for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Message caps:</strong> A $10/month subscription with a 200-message daily limit costs $0.05/message, or $5.00/100 exchanges — matching premium API models.</li>
    <li><strong>Image generation:</strong> Some platforms bundle image generation into the subscription; others charge per image. We separate text and media costs.</li>
    <li><strong>Minimum top-ups:</strong> API credits often require minimum purchases (e.g., $5–10 minimum on OpenRouter) that inflate the effective entry cost.</li>
  </ul>
